// A corpus member for the baseline-aware desk check (general form §6.3).
//
// The published shape — snapshotted into `.ridl/baseline/` beside this file and
// committed — declared its interactions in this order:
//
//   interface VehicleStatus            service corpus.baseline.hvac (inline shape)
//     1  currentSpeed                    1  cabinTemp
//     2  doorOpened                      2  filterClogged
//     3  doorClosed                      3  setEcoMode
//     4  setGear
//     5  reserved legacyWheelPhase
//
// This source drifts from it in five ways, each of which looks like tidying in
// a review diff and each of which moves a wire identity. The five are one per
// change category the desk check reports, so no category's message is left
// without a living example:
//
//   - the two events are alphabetised (a reorder — two of them);
//   - `tyrePressure` is declared above them (an insertion);
//   - `setGear` is retired with no tombstone (a removal);
//   - `legacyWheelPhase` is declared again although the baseline retires the
//     name (a reserved name redeclared);
//   - `setEcoMode` is retired from the *inline shape* with no tombstone.
//
// The last one is the point of the inline shape being here at all. A named
// interface and a service's inline shape are two separate stores of
// interactions, and a consumer that reads only `Package.interfaces` misses the
// second — see `crates/ridlc/tests/corpus/veh-cluster/NOTES`. The desk check
// reports the change either way, but the span it attaches differs, and the
// test beside this file pins that difference.

package corpus.baseline

type Speed     : km/h    [0.0..250.0 step 0.5]
type DoorState : integer [0..1]
type GearIndex : integer [0..6]

interface VehicleStatus {
  signal currentSpeed : Speed @10ms
  event tyrePressure : DoorState @[100ms..1s]
  event doorClosed : DoorState @[100ms..1s]
  event doorOpened : DoorState @[100ms..1s]
  signal legacyWheelPhase : Speed @10ms
}

service corpus.baseline.hvac {
  signal cabinTemp : Speed @[500ms..5s]
  event filterClogged : DoorState @[100ms..1s]
}
